@startuml seq_sel_debounce
title SC-SEL-01 - Selector debounce: change accepted after 50 ms, short glitch ignored

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-SEL-001, SIM-CON-002, SIM-PLT-002
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
SIM_Driver.Selector: 0 = P, 1 = R, 2 = N, 3 = D (can_matrix section 3.1).
end note

note over TCU: control active, mode Normal, vehicle at standstill,\nselector N accepted, 1st prepared: SS_A = ON, SS_B = ON (SYS-SEL-005)

== change N -> D ==
User -> Console : select D
Console -> Plant : selector D
Plant -> Plant : lever in D: engages the gear of SS_A / SS_B = 1st (SIM-PLT-002)
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 3 (D) (t0, first frame with D)
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 3 (D)
end
... Selector = 3 received unchanged for 50 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : t0 + 50 ms: D accepted (SYS-SEL-001)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: SelectorState = 3 (D), GearTarget = 1 (next 100 ms frame)

== glitch shorter than 50 ms ==
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 2 (N) (t1)
note right of TCU: a new position is accepted only after\nit has been received unchanged for 50 ms
... less than 50 ms ...
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 3 (D) again
TCU -> TCU : N not accepted, D kept (SYS-SEL-001)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: SelectorState = 3 (D) unchanged

note over Plant, TCU
After reset the selector position is N until the first position is accepted (SYS-SEL-001), see SC-STA-01.
An invalid value (4 .. 7) for longer than 100 ms is handled in SC-SEL-02.
end note
@enduml
